==============================================================================
M98 S6 -- AXIS control: are M92 and the shipped knob the same knob?
==============================================================================

  shipped   merge.rs:319   admits  best - focus <= T*sqrt(2)*0.015214
                           LARGER T admits MORE frames.  Default 4.0.
  M57/M92   m57lib.py:510  admits  cf >= gate * peak
                           LARGER gate admits FEWER frames.
  They are different acceptance RULES on opposite-running axes, not
  two settings of one knob.  mean n_eff is the only bridge either
  report supplies.

--- shipped-axis n_eff calibration: 112MSDCF half A, 40 frames (M92's stack) ---
