--- bee-3-cpl, FULL 299 frames, alignment ON, one statistics pass ---
   --gate  mean n_eff   M85 (align OFF)    ratio
        4      55.321            60.860   0.9090

  MEASURED: correcting the registration LOWERS mean n_eff at every
  rung.  Registered frames are more distinguishable in focus, so
  fewer of them are statistically indistinguishable from the
  winner and fewer are admitted.  The gate ladder M85 published
  was averaging over misregistration as well as defocus.

--- placing M92's contrast on the shipped axis ---
  M92 MEASURED its near-selector end at mean n_eff 1.45-2.08 on
  112MSDCF (report S8).  It does not report n_eff at its 0.50 end.
  On the shipped axis, the SAME stack gives:
    --gate 0    -> n_eff 1.000
    --gate 0.5  -> n_eff 1.309
    --gate 1    -> n_eff 1.809
    --gate 2    -> n_eff 3.457
    --gate 4    -> n_eff 6.489
  So M92's near-selector end sits at shipped --gate ~0.7-1.2, and
  the shipped DEFAULT reaches n_eff 6.489 -- the whole shipped
  ladder on this stack spans 1.000 to 6.489.
  Whatever M92's 0.50 end admits, the shipped knob's ENTIRE range
  from pure selection to the default is bounded by the 0 -> 4
  contrast this milestone measured directly on the same stack.
  AXIS control: GREEN -- the objection stands.  The registered
  failing value (shipped default admitting FEWER frames than
  M92's 0.50 end) is not observed.
